    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.72) anchor the lineup as our most efficient starts. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Quintana, whose 5.24 xERA is the highest on our board, coupled with a productive #3 hole assignment. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a daily lock despite a tougher draw against Painter; his ability to mitigate platoon disadvantages while maintaining elite order positioning keeps his floor remarkably high. We are also expecting a major contribution from **Taylor Ward** (71.19), who finds himself in a \"green light\" situation: he holds a massive 16% park adjustment and a significant BvP edge against Valdez, helping him climb past lower-tier options despite facing a competent arm.\n\nThe rotation decisions today were dictated by marginal differences in platoon optimization and park factors. **Matt Chapman** (59.53) serves as our most intriguing bench-to-starter consideration; he narrowly missed the 60+ threshold, but his matchup against Schultz\u2014who is surrendering high exit velocities\u2014provided enough upside to justify the UTIL spot over lower-upside bench options. Conversely, **Jonathan Aranda** (44.24) and **Bryson Stott** (40.48) find themselves in the lineup primarily due to game-cap management, despite facing daunting xERA profiles and unfavorable wind conditions. It is worth noting that we are currently navigating a depleted bench, with **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** both on the IL, leaving no room for error if a late lineup scratch occurs. \n\nWe are monitoring **Jeremiah Jackson** (52.61) closely today; while his score is modest, the 100% SB probability correlation with the opponent's delivery time offers a unique \"scarcity play\" that standard projections often undervalue. We remain disciplined in keeping **Lawrence Butler**, **Will Smith**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Drew Gilbert** on the bench, prioritizing the active matchups listed above to maximize our efficiency in the 5x5 categories. Watch the weather reports for the games involving **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman**, as the \"Wind Out\" factor is the only thing keeping those projections in the Strong tier given the opponent's pitching profile.",
